  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5f1214fb30866644fb811b04fa59a1f2, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::InfoOpener
  interactRange: 1.5
  popupController: {fileID: 7154850324694818045}
  titleText: {fileID: 568867888}
  infoText: {fileID: 1737973553}
  titleContent: Slave Trade
  infoContent: Between the 1600s and 1800s, between 12 and 15 million African people
    were taken from their homes by force. Turner's painting on the far left depicts
    a slave ship in a storm, its chaos reflecting the horror of the Middle Passage.
    The diagram shows the Brookes ship, illustrating how human beings were packed
    below deck like cargo for a crossing that took weeks. The map shows the triangular
    trade route connecting Europe, Africa, and the Americas. The shackles on the
    wall were used to restrain captives during the crossing, chained below deck for
    weeks at a time with almost no room to move. An estimated 2 million people did
    not survive the journey.
