  m_EditorClassIdentifier: '::'
  interactRange: 1.5
  popupController: {fileID: 7154850324694818045}
  titleText: {fileID: 568867888}
  infoText: {fileID: 1737973553}
  titleContent: 'Ceremonial Masks '
  infoContent: African masks were among the most important objects a community could
    produce. They were worn during initiation ceremonies, funerals, harvests, and
    in the resolution of disputes. When a person wore a mask they were understood
    to be temporarily inhabited by the spirit it represented. The mask was not a
    costume. It was a transformation. Mask traditions varied widely across the continent
    and each design carried specific meaning within its own culture.
