  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5f1214fb30866644fb811b04fa59a1f2, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::InfoOpener
  interactRange: 1.5
  popupController: {fileID: 7154850324694818045}
  titleText: {fileID: 568867888}
  infoText: {fileID: 1737973553}
  titleContent: Inventors & Innovators
  infoContent: Mae Jemison on the left became the first Black woman in space in 1992,
    a scientist and physician who broke through barriers in both medicine and aerospace.
    The portrait in the centre shows Lewis Latimer, whose development of the carbon
    filament made Edison's lightbulb practical enough for widespread everyday use.
    Without his contribution the lightbulb remains a novelty. Madam C.J. Walker on
    the right built a haircare business empire from nothing and became the first
    self-made female millionaire in American history. All three achieved this while
    navigating systems built to exclude them.
