  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5f1214fb30866644fb811b04fa59a1f2, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::InfoOpener
  interactRange: 1.5
  popupController: {fileID: 7154850324694818045}
  titleText: {fileID: 568867888}
  infoText: {fileID: 1737973553}
  titleContent: 'Music and Metalwork '
  infoContent: The drum was the most important instrument across much of Africa.
    It was used to communicate across long distances, to mark the rhythm of ceremonies,
    and to tell stories. Skilled drummers were respected members of their communities,
    sometimes holding roles equivalent to historians or priests. The iron bracelet
    represents the advanced metalworking traditions of West and Central Africa, where
    smiths were considered to hold spiritual power because of their ability to transform
    raw material into tools, weapons, and art.
