--- !u!114 &1691905978
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1691905977}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5f1214fb30866644fb811b04fa59a1f2, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::InfoOpener
  interactRange: 1.5
  popupController: {fileID: 7154850324694818045}
  titleText: {fileID: 568867888}
  infoText: {fileID: 1737973553}
  titleContent: Sculptures
  infoContent: Every object in this collection was made with purpose. The divided
    face represents duality, the balance between life and death, the physical and
    the spiritual. The bull reflects the significance of cattle across East and Southern
    Africa, where a man's herd defined his standing in society. The portrait head
    comes from a tradition in the Yoruba city of Ife, where sculptors depicted kings
    with remarkable realism as far back as the 12th century. The standing figure
    is a carved wooden form typical of Central and West African traditions, made
    to honour ancestors and mark important spiritual and communal roles. None of
    this was decoration. Every piece carried the history of the people who made it.
