  interactRange: 1.5
  popupController: {fileID: 7154850324694818045}
  titleText: {fileID: 568867888}
  infoText: {fileID: 1737973553}
  titleContent: The Modern Era
  infoContent: Barack Obama became the 44th President of the United States in 2008,
    the first Black person to hold the office. Ketanji Brown Jackson became the first
    Black woman appointed to the United States Supreme Court in 2022. Kendrick Lamar
    became the first rapper to win the Pulitzer Prize for Music in 2018. The Grammy
    beside this plaque represents a music industry built significantly on Black artistry,
    from jazz and blues to hip hop and R&B, genres that changed what popular music
    sounds like across the entire world.
