  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5f1214fb30866644fb811b04fa59a1f2, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::InfoOpener
  interactRange: 1.5
  popupController: {fileID: 7154850324694818045}
  titleText: {fileID: 568867888}
  infoText: {fileID: 1737973553}
  titleContent: Leaders & Trailblazers
  infoContent: Nelson Mandela spent 27 years imprisoned in South Africa rather than
    abandon his opposition to apartheid, and went on to lead the country's transition
    to democracy and serve as its first Black president. Rosa Parks refused to give
    up her bus seat in Montgomery, Alabama in 1955, an act that sparked a 381 day
    boycott and directly challenged the segregation laws that governed daily life
    across the American South. The third portrait represents the generations of leaders
    and activists whose names are less known but whose courage made every visible
    victory possible.
