  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5f1214fb30866644fb811b04fa59a1f2, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::InfoOpener
  interactRange: 1.5
  popupController: {fileID: 7154850324694818045}
  titleText: {fileID: 568867888}
  infoText: {fileID: 1737973553}
  titleContent: Plantation Life
  infoContent: Enslaved people in the American South worked from before sunrise to
    after sunset with no pay and no freedom, growing cotton, tobacco, and sugar that
    built enormous wealth for others. The paintings here show scenes of daily life
    under slavery, from labour in the fields to quieter moments within enslaved communities.
    Despite conditions designed to strip them of everything, enslaved people maintained
    rich internal cultures, holding onto music, language, and traditions that connected
    them to their African roots. Resistance was constant and took many forms.
