  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5f1214fb30866644fb811b04fa59a1f2, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::InfoOpener
  interactRange: 1.5
  popupController: {fileID: 7154850324694818045}
  titleText: {fileID: 568867888}
  infoText: {fileID: 1737973553}
  titleContent: Harlem Renaissance
  infoContent: The three figures in this display represent the cultural explosion
    that transformed Black American life in the 1920s and 30s. Billie Holiday on
    the left became one of the most influential jazz and blues singers in history,
    her voice carrying a depth of feeling that stopped audiences completely. The
    painting in the centre is from Aaron Douglas, whose bold visual style rooted
    in African identity defined the visual art of the Harlem Renaissance. Langston
    Hughes on the right was one of the greatest American poets of the 20th century,
    giving the Black experience a literary voice that the whole world heard.
